meta {
  name: Refund All (Combined)
  type: http
  seq: 43
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/refund-all
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "allocations": [
      { "orderId": "{{subOrderDiagnosticId}}", "amount": 350 },
      { "orderId": "{{subOrderRadiologyId}}", "amount": 150 }
    ],
    "paymentMode": "CASH"
  }
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  Refund across a combined order's CHILD sub-orders in a single atomic transaction
  (Registration/Finance → Billings → "Refund All"). `:id` may be the PARENT order
  or either CHILD. Requires the `REG_UPDATE_REFUND_AMOUNT` permission. All amounts
  are rupees (up to 2 decimal places).

  Body:
  - `allocations` (required, ≥1 entry) — per-sub-order refunds:
    `[{ "orderId": "<child id>", "amount": 350, "refundCharge": 0 }, ...]`.
    `amount` (≥0) is returned to the patient — a 0 amount skips that sub-order;
    `refundCharge?` (≥0, default 0) is a fee the lab retains. At least one entry
    must have a positive `amount`.
  - `paymentMode` (required) — how the refunds are paid back.
  - `reference?`, `paymentDate?` (ISO) — optional.

  Each sub-order is validated INDEPENDENTLY against its own refundable balance and
  its branch's Cancellation & Refund settings — exactly like `POST /orders/:id/refund`:
  - `AllowRefund` off ⇒ 422 `REFUND_NOT_ALLOWED`.
  - nothing refundable on a sub-order ⇒ 422 `NOTHING_TO_REFUND`.
  - `amount + refundCharge` exceeds that sub-order's refundable balance ⇒ 422
    `REFUND_EXCEEDS_REFUNDABLE`.
  - `AllowPartialRefund` off ⇒ `amount` must equal the full refundable-to-patient
    (`refundable − refundCharge`), else 422 `PARTIAL_REFUND_NOT_ALLOWED`.
  - `RefundChargesApplicable` off ⇒ `refundCharge` ignored (forced to 0); on ⇒
    used or defaults to the configured `RefundChargesAmount`.

  Nothing is written if any sub-order fails validation (the whole transaction rolls
  back). Other failures: 422 `COMBINED_PAYMENT_INVALID` (no positive refund amount),
  422 `SUB_ORDER_NOT_IN_PARENT` (an `orderId` not under this parent), 422
  `NOT_A_COMBINED_ORDER` / 404 `ORDER_NOT_FOUND`.

  Writes one REFUND `PaymentDetails` row per refunded sub-order (append-only — prior
  payments are never overwritten), recomputes each sub-order's `paymentStatus` /
  `refundStatus` / `billStatus`, then re-aggregates the PARENT once. Returns the
  parent's sub-orders, fully composed, with their new balances.

  NOTE: set `{{subOrderDiagnosticId}}` / `{{subOrderRadiologyId}}` from a prior
  `GET /orders/:id/sub-orders` response (the CHILD ids), and `{{orderId}}` to the
  combined order's parent or child id.
}
